## 2. New Rules — v1.1.0-preview

### FR-007: Enhanced Plaintext Credential Regex Scan

**Purpose**: Expand credential scanning beyond JSON files to ALL file types in factor_workspace. Covers Python scripts, config files, CSV exports, and text logs that may contain leaked credentials.

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Rule ID | FR-007 |
| Name | `enhanced_plaintext_credential_scan` |
| Severity | CRITICAL |
| Action | `alert_and_log` |
| Scope | `factor_workspace/**/*` (ALL file types) |
| Max file size for scan | 10 MB |
| Excluded | `*.pyc`, `*.pyo`, `*.so`, `*.dll` |

**Patterns**:
- AWS access key ID: `AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}`
- GitHub personal access token: `ghp_[a-zA-Z0-9]{36}`
- GitHub OAuth token: `gho_[a-zA-Z0-9]{36}`
- OpenAI/SendGrid API key: `sk-[a-zA-Z0-9]{20,}`
- Generic API key pattern: `(?i)(api[_-]?key|apikey|secret|token|password|passwd|pwd)\s*[:=]\s*['\"][^'\"]+['\"]`
- Private key header: `-----BEGIN (RSA |EC |DSA |OPENSSH )?PRIVATE KEY-----`
- Slack token: `xox[baprs]-[a-zA-Z0-9-]+`
- Telegram bot token: `([0-9]{8,10}):[a-zA-Z0-9_-]{35}`
- Stripe secret key: `sk_live_[a-zA-Z0-9]{24,48}`

**Safety**: No file modification. Alerts logged to `opt_hooks/factor_runtime_alert_log.txt` and `opt_hooks/factor_runtime_alerts.json`. Manual escalation required.

### FR-008: Short-Time Batch File Generation Alert

**Purpose**: Detect anomalous rapid file creation patterns that may indicate runaway factor computation loops, data corruption, or unintended mass generation.

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Rule ID | FR-008 |
| Name | `short_time_batch_generation_alert` |
| Severity | WARNING |
| Action | `alert` |
| Scope | `factor_workspace/**/*` |

**Detection logic**:

| Metric | Threshold | Critical |
|--------|:---------:|:--------:|
| Files created in 60s window | >100 | >500 |
| Files created in 300s window | >500 | >2000 |
| Files created in 1800s window | >2000 | >10000 |
| Single directory creation rate | >50 files/60s | >200 files/60s |
| Total new bytes in 60s | >10 MB | >100 MB |

**Safety**: Observe-alert only. Does NOT delete files, kill processes, or modify outputs. Alerts logged and require manual review.

### FR-009: Output Directory Whitelist

**Purpose**: Explicit whitelist of allowed output directories within factor_workspace. Any file written outside these directories triggers an alert.

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Rule ID | FR-009 |
| Name | `output_directory_whitelist` |
| Severity | WARNING |
| Action | `alert` |
| Scope | `factor_workspace/` root |

**Allowed output directories**:
```
factor_workspace/pb_zn_recyclepb_v1/input/
factor_workspace/pb_zn_recyclepb_v1/output/
factor_workspace/pb_zn_recyclepb_v1/audit/
factor_workspace/pb_zn_recyclepb_v1/checksum/
```

**Forbidden output patterns**:
- Any path containing `..` (directory traversal)
- Any path outside `factor_workspace/`
- Any path within `scripts/`, `framework-tree/scripts/`
- Any path within archived directories (`*_ARCHIVED/`)
- Any path within `p012_nativepass_consolidate/`
- Any path within `opt-phase04-psutil-collector/`

**Safety**: Alert only. Does NOT block writes or modify the filesystem. Boundary violations are logged for manual review.

